Cell["\<\
The agreement is limited by NIntegrate, not by the spectral method: 19 basis \
functions are far more than needed at \[Gamma] = 0.5.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e7303f40-f0d0-4650-8a93-7894e0e9d352"]
}, Closed]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Reading \[Mu] from the package", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"1e1052ba-4a3b-4ed8-8200-ce953328ff33"],

Cell["\<\
You don't need to keep your own eigensolver. Ask \
SpinWeightedSpheroidalHarmonicS for the \"SphericalExpansion\" method and \
read its \"Coefficients\". Three details:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"55a8903c-59d6-4911-8a96-b437d7e39964"],

Cell["\<\
For a numerical \[Gamma] the default method is \"Leaver\", whose stored \
coefficients are Leaver's series coefficients, not \[Mu]. Always pass Method \
-> {\"SphericalExpansion\", \"NumTerms\" -> n}.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"ab7bf044-a7d5-4584-b9fd-b56d1a222490"],

Cell["\<\
The coefficients for S_\[ScriptL]' cover \[ScriptL] = \[ScriptL]' - nDown \
\[Ellipsis] \[ScriptL]' + n with nDown = Min[\[ScriptL]' - \[ScriptL]min, n] \
and \[ScriptL]min = Max[|s|, |m|]. So different columns start at different \
\[ScriptL] and have to be padded with zeros into a common row range.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"e9bc9c35-7214-4f31-bcbf-1f04c2ecc4a0"],

Cell["\<\
At \[Gamma] = 0 exactly the package switches to method \"SphericalExact\" and \
stores no coefficients: return the unit vector (since S(0)=Y).\
\>", "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.003922477527298*^9, 4.003922484097397*^9}, {
  4.00392252493334*^9, 
  4.003922526598329*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"ee36e1dd-e2f7-43b8-89ef-\
3cae56c9a801"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Exercise 4", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"90d78c2d-d5ca-4a04-a1b3-c12438fb254c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Goal: replace your own eigensolver from Exercise 3 with the package's. \
SpinWeightedSpheroidalHarmonicS with Method -> {\"SphericalExpansion\", \
\"NumTerms\" -> n} already returns the Y-components of one S_\[ScriptL]', \
that is, one column of \[Mu]*. It stores them on its own \[ScriptL] window, \
though (see the three details above). Wrap it into a matrix with the layout \
of muSpec (rows \[ScriptL], columns \[ScriptL]'). Sections 5\[Dash]7 use this \
matrix.\n\n* Essentially when calling SpinWeightedSpheroidalHarmonicS with \
Method -> {\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]SphericalExpansion\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]NumTerms\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] -> n} the coefficient \
list are the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[Mu]", "lm"], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "0f50599a-1794-448a-a430-329e1c54956e"],
 " such that, for a given pair (l,m) ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["S", "lm"], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        SubscriptBox["\[Mu]", 
         RowBox[{"l0", " ", "l"}]], 
        SubscriptBox["Y", 
         RowBox[{"0", " ", "lm"}]]}], "+", 
       RowBox[{
        SubscriptBox["\[Mu]", 
         RowBox[{"l0", "+", 
          RowBox[{"1", "l"}]}]], 
        SubscriptBox["Y", 
         RowBox[{"l0", "+", 
          RowBox[{"1", "m"}]}]]}], "+"}], "..."}], "+", 
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox["\[Mu]", 
       RowBox[{"lmax", " ", "l"}]], 
      SubscriptBox["Y", 
       RowBox[{"lmax", " ", "m"}]]}]}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "a7112ae6-b4c6-483f-938e-b69b4da50e8c"],
 " "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.003922558975339*^9, 4.003922720679077*^9}, {
  4.003922755937812*^9, 4.003922779201672*^9}, {4.0039228381507387`*^9, 
  4.0039228517175913`*^9}, {4.003922946644994*^9, 4.00392297873103*^9}, {
  4.003923202540189*^9, 
  4.003923203281767*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"48a7d9d5-7663-4c72-ad05-\
75272db4af1e"],

Cell["\<\
(a) muCol[lp, m, \[Gamma], lmaxRow, n] returns column \[ScriptL]' = lp of \
\[Mu] on the fixed rows \[ScriptL] = \[ScriptL]min\[Ellipsis]lmaxRow. Read \
the coefficients and place them at \[ScriptL] = l0 \[Ellipsis] l0 + Length - \
1, with l0 = lp - Min[lp - \[ScriptL]min, n]. Here lmin is Max[2,Abs[m]] and \
Length is the number of coefficients computed by SphericalExpansion. Put \
zeros everywhere else and drop rows beyond lmaxRow. At \[Gamma] = 0, return \
the unit vector. n sets the accuracy of the package's computation; lmaxRow \
only sets how many rows you keep.\
\>", "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.0039246982895813`*^9, 
  4.00392472558237*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"bed478de-f13f-489a-b5a6-\
c47cda618340"],

Cell["\<\
muMatrix[m, \[Gamma], lmaxRow, lmaxCol, n] puts the columns \[ScriptL]' = \
\[ScriptL]min\[Ellipsis]lmaxCol side by side. It is rectangular: take lmaxRow \
> lmaxCol when you need the leakage into higher \[ScriptL] (Exercise 2).\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"d33d5a36-a84b-4469-86e1-760c4c02ad29"],

Cell["\<\
Check: compare muMatrix[2, g, 6, 6] with muSpec[[1;;5, 1;;5]]. If they agree, \
the package also uses your sign convention (positive diagonal).\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"aef5e18b-879d-4044-8cea-0224273a4c97"],

Cell["\<\
(b) Convergence in n: compare n = 10 with n = 20, keeping the same rows and \
columns. The difference measures the package's own truncation error on the \
entries you keep.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"26f6209f-79f4-40ec-af85-b2d331ed4a06"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
(c) Worst case. \[Mu] moves away from the identity when \[Gamma] = a m \
\[CapitalOmega] is large: at \[Chi] = 0.998, at the ISCO, and at m = lmax = \
8. Compute that \[Gamma] (r_ISCO from KerrGeoISCO, \[CapitalOmega] = \
1/(r^{3/2} + a)), build \[Mu] with rows up to about 24 and columns up to \
about 14, and plot |\[Mu]_\[ScriptL]\[ScriptL]'| against \[ScriptL] for a few \
columns \[ScriptL]'. Since C_\[ScriptL]m = \[CapitalSigma]_\[ScriptL]' \[Mu]_\
\[ScriptL]\[ScriptL]' C^up_\[ScriptL]'m, the width of the band around the \
diagonal tells you how many spheroidal \[ScriptL]' beyond \[ScriptL] feed a \
given spherical \[ScriptL]. How many \[ScriptL]' beyond lmax do you need for \
\[ScriptL] = lmax?\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"c5be973a-7fb5-43bf-99fa-a58d6669b7e5"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"SpinWeightedSpheroidalHarmonicS", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"-", "2"}], ",", "8", ",", "4", ",", "0.5", ",", 
     RowBox[{"Method", "->", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<SphericalExpansion\>\"", ",", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<NumTerms\>\"", "->", "3"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}], "[", 
   "\"\<ExpansionCoefficients\>\"", "]"}], "//", "Length"}]], "Input",
