Cell["\<\
(3,2): ratio 1.2-1.5, roughly a line through the origin: the shift is a \
0.5PN-relative spin effect, \[Proportional] \[Chi] v. The ratio grows with \
\[Chi] v (higher orders in \[Gamma]), and at \[Chi] = 0.998 the relative \
change exceeds 1: the spherical (3,2) is almost all leakage from (2,2). \
(2,2): ratio 0.04-0.14, so \[Proportional] \[Chi] v^5 up to the O(\[Gamma]^2) \
term of (b).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"431e1a48-1bba-471e-8586-9742fa130116"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"d6i", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"amps", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<a0.9_isco\>\"", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"N", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
          RowBox[{"toSpherical", "[", 
           RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"d6i", "[", "\"\<gamma\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"d6i", "[", "\"\<Cup\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", "14"}], "]"}],
           "]"}], "^", "2"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
          RowBox[{"toSpherical", "[", 
           RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"d6i", "[", "\"\<gamma\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"d6i", "[", "\"\<Cup\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", "8"}], "]"}], 
          "]"}], "^", "2"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "/", 
     RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
        RowBox[{"d6i", "[", "\"\<Cup\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], "^", "2"}], "]"}]}], 
    " ", "-", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}]}], "Input",ExpressionUUID->\
"b93d25c1-507d-4c5f-aa38-48bbc891f7dc"],

Cell["\<\
Rows up to 14: equal to working precision. Rows up to 8: the missing power is \
~1e-18. The flux is basis independent (notes Section 3), so the flux grid \
stays as it is; only amplitudes and phases need the change of basis. For m < \
0 nothing new: C_{l,-m} = (-1)^l C*_{lm} in the spherical basis, so compute m \
> 0 only.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ccf5547c-c2fc-4af8-ac6f-18af6dd3e684"]
}, Closed]]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["7. Truncation in l'", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"8da5a4fb-e2d2-4238-97b6-30f98310ad71"],

Cell["\<\
Physics: notes Section 4. Three different cuts appear: the package's NumTerms \
(harmless), the rows l \[LessEqual] L you keep (a modelling choice that does \
not change any kept C_lm), and the columns l' \[LessEqual] L' you computed. \
Only the last one is an error on the amplitudes you keep: C_lm misses \
\[CapitalSigma]_{l' > L'} \[Mu]_{l l'} Cup_l'm (notes eq. 10).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0599a46f-4295-494b-a680-1d373cbea3ea"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Exercise 7", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"ff707f34-ee65-48f3-90d0-f63ef738600c"],

Cell["\<\
Question: where does cutting the spheroidal sum hurt, and how many extra \
spheroidal modes does the grid rerun need? Keep the rows fixed at l \
\[LessEqual] L = 8 throughout, so only the columns L' = L + \[CapitalDelta] \
change. The reference is all stored columns (l' \[LessEqual] 14); \
errTrunc[key, m, L, L'] gives the relative error of every row.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f5a04bd0-9b3f-45c4-a8d5-a98e68c47e7c"],

Cell["\<\
(a) Orbit \"a0.9_isco\", m = 2. Plot the relative error against l for \
\[CapitalDelta] = 0, 1, 2, 4. Where is the error, and how much does each \
extra spheroidal mode buy?\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"6ae1b724-3448-4bfe-b11f-57938a1e89c6"],

Cell["\<\
(b) Error model. The first omitted spheroidal mode contributes \[Mu]_{l,L'+1} \
Cup_{L'+1}. Compute it (one column of muM times one amplitude) and compare \
with the true error from (a). What does this give you for free on every grid \
node?\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"fcf4b6af-3af1-42a5-aed6-62dbf1e45f46"],

Cell["\<\
(c) Worst case. For every orbit and m = 2, 4, 6, 8, compute the error at l = \
L with \[CapitalDelta] = 0 and plot it against |\[Gamma]_m|. Which (orbit, m) \
is worst? Why is the trend clean for m = 8 but not for m = 2 (notes Section \
4, item 3)?\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"c3c719d5-bef1-4f6b-aa8d-cc106daf6668"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
(d) Decide. Which \[CapitalDelta] keeps the worst case below 1e-4 \
(interpolation error of the current 18x27 grid, benchmarks.md) and below \
1e-10 (Honet's refined grid)? This \[CapitalDelta] goes into Section 8.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"609f3e2a-04a9-4430-8df6-1c6a2b703d1a"],

Cell[BoxData[""], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"c9d3f21d-eeeb-424e-9dc8-efa4f2786732"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Solution", "Subsubsection",ExpressionUUID->"67550c2b-898d-400c-bde8-a595f6da169f"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"L", " ", "=", " ", "8"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"ListLogPlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
         RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "L"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"errTrunc", "[", 
         RowBox[{
         "\"\<a0.9_isco\>\"", ",", " ", "2", ",", " ", "L", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"L", " ", "+", " ", "dl"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", 
     " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"dl", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "2", ",", " ", "4"}], "}"}]}], 
      "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Joined", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotMarkers", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
     "\"\<\[CapitalDelta] = 0\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<\[CapitalDelta] = 1\>\"", 
      ",", " ", "\"\<\[CapitalDelta] = 2\>\"", ",", " ", 
      "\"\<\[CapitalDelta] = 4\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"AxesLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<l\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<rel. error\>\""}], "}"}]}]}], 
  "]"}]}], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"3fba5d0b-8397-4b61-90d1-b5d321e76742"],

Cell["\<\
The error sits in the top row l = L: one row lower it is 4 orders smaller. \
Each extra spheroidal mode buys 2-4 orders.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"93c37986-56b3-4360-b7a1-880bd0558cc2"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"estTrunc", "[", 
    RowBox[{"key_", ",", " ", "m_", ",", " ", "L_", ",", " ", "Lp_"}], "]"}], 
   " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"d", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"amps", "[", 
         RowBox[{"key", ",", " ", "m"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"lmin", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
         RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "m"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"muM", "[", 
         RowBox[{"m", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"d", "[", "\"\<gamma\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", "L", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Lp", " ", "+", " ", "1"}]}], "]"}], "[", 
        RowBox[{"[", 
         RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"d", "[", "\"\<Cup\>\"", "]"}], "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", 
          RowBox[{"Lp", " ", "+", " ", "2", " ", "-", " ", "lmin"}], "]"}], 
         "]"}], "/", 
        RowBox[{"cTrunc", "[", 
         RowBox[{"key", ",", " ", "m", ",", " ", "L", ",", " ", "14"}], 
         "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"TableForm", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
       RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "L"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"N", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"errTrunc", "[", 
         RowBox[{
         "\"\<a0.9_isco\>\"", ",", " ", "2", ",", " ", "L", ",", " ", "L"}], 
         "]"}], ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"N", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"estTrunc", "[", 
         RowBox[{
         "\"\<a0.9_isco\>\"", ",", " ", "2", ",", " ", "L", ",", " ", "L"}], 
         "]"}], ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"TableHeadings", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"None", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
       "\"\<l\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<true error\>\"", ",", " ", 
        "\"\<one-term estimate\>\""}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",Ex\
pressionUUID->"27d2a886-12e2-4b22-91e0-f858fd76ebde"],

Cell["\<\
The one-term estimate matches the true error in every row. So on the grid, \
compute one spheroidal mode more than you use: its contribution is a \
node-by-node error estimate at no extra cost.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ffed903d-e0fa-4afe-88ac-bbc9a02766b2"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"worst", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Flatten", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"amps", "[", 
            RowBox[{"k", ",", " ", "mm"}], "]"}], "[", "\"\<gamma\>\"", "]"}],
           "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Last", "[", 
          RowBox[{"errTrunc", "[", 
           RowBox[{"k", ",", " ", "mm", ",", " ", "L", ",", " ", "L"}], "]"}],
           "]"}], ",", " ", "k", ",", " ", "mm"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"k", ",", " ", "orbits"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"mm", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "4", ",", " ", "6", ",", " ", "8"}], "}"}]}],
         "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"ListLogPlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Select", "[", 
       RowBox[{"worst", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"#", "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", "4", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", "mm"}], " ", 
         "&"}]}], "]"}], "[", 
      RowBox[{"[", 
       RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"mm", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "4", ",", " ", "6", ",", " ", "8"}], "}"}]}], 
      "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotMarkers", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
     "\"\<m = 2\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<m = 4\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<m = 6\>\"", 
      ",", " ", "\"\<m = 8\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"AxesLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
     "\"\<|\[Gamma]_m|\>\"", ",", " ", 
      "\"\<error at l = L, \[CapitalDelta] = 0\>\""}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"N", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Take", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"SortBy", "[", 
      RowBox[{"worst", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", 
         RowBox[{"#", "[", 
          RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}]}], " ", "&"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     "3"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}]}], "Input",ExpressionUUID->\
"0d39cbaa-4459-4d9a-8181-aa3e094970a6"],

Cell["\<\
Worst: l = m = 8 at \[Chi] = 0.998 near the ISCO, about 1e-2. At m = L the \
only kept mode, l = m, is the loudest of its m and sits at the cut, so the \
error grows cleanly with \[Gamma]. For m < L the denominator C_Lm is itself \
fed by louder modes below, so a larger \[Gamma] can lower the relative error \
(m = 2 at \[Chi] = 0.998 is smaller than at \[Chi] = 0.9).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"442c84c7-de45-43d3-aa02-2805c4cbf119"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"TableForm", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"dl", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"N", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
          RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"Last", "[", 
             RowBox[{"errTrunc", "[", 
              RowBox[{"k", ",", " ", "mm", ",", " ", "L", ",", " ", 
               RowBox[{"L", " ", "+", " ", "dl"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{"k", ",", " ", "orbits"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{"mm", ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"{", 
               RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "4", ",", " ", "6", ",", " ", "8"}], 
               "}"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}]}], 
      "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"dl", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "4"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   
   RowBox[{"TableHeadings", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"None", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
       "\"\<\[CapitalDelta]\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<worst error at l = L\>\""}], 
       "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"783af4a3-7066-\
4e9a-940b-be09de1173f5"],

Cell["\<\
\[CapitalDelta] = 1 already gives 4e-5 < 1e-4; take \[CapitalDelta] = 2 \
(4e-7) for margin on the current grid. \[CapitalDelta] = 3 gives 1.6e-9, so \
the refined grid needs \[CapitalDelta] = 4 (7e-12).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4032924f-86c2-4c4d-a67a-c90924a7f511"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Your attempt at the old Exercise 6 (kept for reference)", \
"Subsubsection",ExpressionUUID->"2ff1b849-a5a8-4cef-95f8-c1b464622954"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"a", "=", "0.9`30"}], ";"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"r0", "=", "4`30"}], ";"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"orb", "=", 
    RowBox[{"KerrGeoOrbit", "[", 
     RowBox[{"a", ",", "r0", ",", "0", ",", "1"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], 
  "\[IndentingNewLine]"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"m", "=", "2"}], ";"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"lmin", "=", 
   RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
    RowBox[{"2", ",", 
     RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "m", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 

 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"lmax", "=", "6"}], ";"}], "\n"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"modes", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"TeukolskyPointParticleMode", "[", 
      RowBox[{"s", ",", "l", ",", "m", ",", "orb"}], "]"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"l", ",", "lmin", ",", "lmax"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"\[Gamma]", "=", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"modes", "[", 
       RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], "[", "\"\<AngularFunction\>\"", "]"}], 
     "[", 
     RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], "[", "\"\<\[Gamma]\>\"", "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\[Mu]", "=", 
    RowBox[{"muMatrix", "[", 
     RowBox[{"m", ",", "\[Gamma]", ",", "lmax", ",", "lmax", ",", "15"}], 
     "]"}]}], ";"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Cspheroidal", "[", 
    RowBox[{"lp_", ",", "m_"}], "]"}], ":=", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"modes", "[", 
      RowBox[{"[", 
       RowBox[{"lp", "-", "lmin", "+", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}], "[", 
     "\"\<Amplitudes\>\"", "]"}], "[", "\"\<\[ScriptCapitalI]\>\"", "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"CspheroidalVec", "=", 
   RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Cspheroidal", "[", 
      RowBox[{"lp", ",", "m"}], "]"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"lp", ",", "lmin", ",", "lmax"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"CsphericalVec", "=", 
   RowBox[{"\[Mu]", ".", "CspheroidalVec"}]}], ";"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Cspherical", "[", "l_", "]"}], ":=", 
    RowBox[{"CsphericalVec", "[", 
     RowBox[{"[", 
      RowBox[{"l", "-", "lmin", "+", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], 
  "\[IndentingNewLine]"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"hlmVec", "=", 
   FractionBox[
    RowBox[{"2", " ", "CsphericalVec"}], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"\[Gamma]", "/", "a"}], ")"}], "2"]]}], ";"}]}], "Input",
