Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["8. Toward the Honet grid (no solution: this is your code)", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"cdce1104-9f6f-4d01-9448-422427f96d97"],

Cell["\<\
What the production code needs, per Chebyshev node (i, j) of FluxesGrid.nb \
and per m = 1 \[Ellipsis] lmax:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"926f8871-25b3-4e87-8a94-ba73335cc755"],

Cell["\<\
New data: the flux grid stores only fluxes. Rerun the grid (same nodeOrbit, \
same precision ladder) and keep md[\"Amplitudes\"][\"\[ScriptCapitalI]\"] \
(and \"\[ScriptCapitalH]\" if you want horizon amplitudes) for l' up to lmax \
+ \[CapitalDelta], with \[CapitalDelta] from Exercise 7d (2 for the current \
grid, 4 for 1e-10), plus one more l' as an error estimate (Exercise 7b).\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"1dfd9261-13f5-4839-857e-16d5542d052e"],

Cell["\<\
\[Gamma]_m from the mode (= m\[Chi]\[CapitalOmega]\:0302_ij with \
\[CapitalOmega]\:0302_ij = (\[Chi]_j + (2r*/(r_C,i + 1))^{3/2})^{-1}, Honet \
(A27)), and the \[Mu] matrix from muMatrix. Check NumTerms convergence at the \
worst node.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"6ff3e688-c2ef-4077-90cd-c671b23a498d"],

Cell["C_\[ScriptL]m = \[Mu] . C_\[ScriptL]'m (A27), keeping \[ScriptL] \
\[LessEqual] lmax.", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"ffd3b899-6a3c-4e82-8a74-\
f7cddf3f1ee7"],

Cell["\<\
Rescale before interpolating: c_\[ScriptL]m = r_p^{\[ScriptL]/2} \
C_\[ScriptL]m/\[CapitalOmega]\:0302\.b2 for \[ScriptL] + m even, r_p^{(1+\
\[ScriptL])/2} C_\[ScriptL]m/\[CapitalOmega]\:0302\.b2 for \[ScriptL] + m \
odd, with r_p = 2r*/(r_C + 1) (A28, A29). Then use the Chebyshev machinery of \
FluxInterpolation.wl.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"b5d601bd-96a2-46aa-bdd9-672e66e761a0"],

Cell["\<\
Reconstruct C_\[ScriptL]m(\[CapitalOmega]\:0302, \[Chi]) with (A30, A31), and \
the real amplitudes \:0125_\[ScriptL]m and phases \[Delta]\[CurlyPhi]_\
\[ScriptL]m with (52)-(54).\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"75ccec13-9ca1-40ac-89ea-c6f623b292bd"],

Cell["\<\
Decide the retrograde convention (Section 5) before you define phases.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"6cb2ead5-2297-464b-b823-c7cc7aeea9c0"],

Cell["\<\
Further reading if you want the derivations: S. A. Hughes, PRD 61, 084004 \
(2000), appendix on the spectral method for spheroidal harmonics; G. B. Cook \
and M. Zalutskiy, PRD 90, 124021 (2014), for the Clebsch\[Dash]Gordan form of \
the matrix and the sign conventions.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9fc9486c-7034-467d-95c1-5ce179e0a5f7"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]]
},
